+        // Companion: the spell's success CHANCE as a whole percent, i.e. the second half of the
+        // vanilla magic menu's "Cost/Chance" column. Read-only, so it takes a plain Object rather
+        // than SelfObject and can be called for any actor.
+        //
+        // Bound rather than reimplemented in Lua on purpose. MWMechanics::getSpellSuccessChance
+        // folds in the per-effect base-cost loop, the lowest-school-skill search, willpower/luck,
+        // the Sound and Silence magic effects, the fatigue term, god mode, the magicka check and
+        // the always-succeed flag -- and its spell-cost term has an autocalc branch that pulls in
+        // calcEffectCost as well. Every input is Lua-readable, but a hand-written copy would be a
+        // long formula with many chances to drift silently out of step with the engine, for a
+        // number the player compares directly against the vanilla screen.
+        //
+        // Defaults are left alone (cap = true, checkMagicka = true) because that is exactly how
+        // MWGui::SpellModel builds mCostColumn, so this matches the vanilla display 1:1 -- including
+        // reading 0 when the player cannot currently afford the spell.
+        actor["getSpellSuccessChance"] = [](const Object& o, const sol::object& spellOrId) -> int {
+            const MWWorld::Ptr& ptr = o.ptr();
+            if (!ptr.getClass().isActor())
+                throw std::runtime_error("Actor expected");
+            return static_cast<int>(MWMechanics::getSpellSuccessChance(toSpellId(spellOrId), ptr));
+        };
